--- !u!114 &2974630881881875856
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 2674590779597219017}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 367689ee5044f384f90357a5791dcf2e, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::JournalItem
  journalText: "Medical Notes \r\nNeema Abercrombie \r\nPatient: Samuel Abercrombie
    \r\nAge: 13 \r\n29 October \r\nRecurring nightmares. Patient reports seeing an
    unidentified \r\nfigure outside the bedroom door.  \r\n\u25CF Sleep disturbance
    \r\n\u25CF  Occasional night terrors  \r\n\u25CF Elevated anxiety.  \r\n\u25CF
    No apparent physical abnormalities. \r\nRecommended increased supervision and
    a regular sleeping \r\nschedule. \r\n4 November \r\nFurther examination required.
    \r\nPatient has developed unusual tenderness along the lower \r\nspine. No visible
    injury or bruising. Temperature fluctuating \r\nwithout apparent cause. \r\nPatient
    claims something is growing beneath his skin. \r\n11 November \r\nI examined
    Samuel again this evening. \r\nThere are several raised structures along the
    lower back. \r\nThey are hard to the touch and appear to follow the \r\nvertebral
    column. \r\nI have never encountered anything resembling this in my \r\nnursing
    experience. \r\nHamish insists it is connected to the nightmares. \r\nI have
    advised him to stop discussing the matter in Samuel's \r\npresence. \r\n18 November
    \r\nSamuel refuses to eat at the dining table; He says the food \r\nsmells wrong.
    He has begun referring to himself in the third \r\nperson. When I asked him why,
    he replied: \"Because that's \r\nnot me anymore.\" \r\nI do not know what to
    do. \r\n30 November \r\nI am his mother. \r\nWhatever happens, I am his mother.
    \r\nI cannot keep him locked downstairs. \r\nI cannot bear to hear him calling
    for me. \r\nGod forgive us."
