--- !u!114 &5220613346728824872
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 2478841469872813534}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 367689ee5044f384f90357a5791dcf2e, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::JournalItem
  journalText: "Dear Neema, \r\nI hope this letter finds you well. I know it's been
    a little while \r\nsince we last spoke, but I thought I'd write rather than keep
    \r\nbothering you with telephone calls. \r\nHave you heard what people have been
    saying about your \r\nfamily? \r\nI don't mean to upset you, but there has been
    some rather \r\nunpleasant gossip circulating in town. Apparently, someone saw
    \r\nHamish walking around the garden in the middle of the night. \r\nOld Mrs
    Fletcher claims she heard a child screaming from your \r\nproperty last Tuesday,
    although I wouldn't put much stock in \r\nanything that woman says. \r\nThere
    are also rumours about Samuel. I heard from someone at \r\nthe hospital that
    you've been bringing him in rather frequently. \r\nI hope the poor boy isn't
    seriously ill. \r\nYou know how people are; give them something they don't \r\nunderstand,
    and they'll invent a dozen explanations. \r\nAnyway, I was thinking of visiting
    next Sunday. It would be \r\nlovely to see the children again, especially Jimmy.
    Last time I \r\nsaw him, he was taller than Hamish! \r\nPlease write back when
    you can. \r\nAll my love, \r\nHelen"
