--- !u!114 &8366952609067242449
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 6064970360741134094}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 367689ee5044f384f90357a5791dcf2e, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::JournalItem
  journalText: "Journal \r\n12 September 2006 - 1 October 2006 \r\nHamish Abercrombie
    \r\n12 September \r\nNeema thinks I spend too much time at my desk. She says
    \r\nthe children need their father, not another book about dead \r\nmen and imaginary
    worlds. \r\nPerhaps she's right. \r\nJames has been doing those dreadful mathematics
    exercises \r\nagain. He showed me something concerning prime numbers \r\nat breakfast,
    which I pretended to understand. The boy is \r\nfrighteningly clever. Tulia has
    taken an interest in painting, \r\nalthough she insists that everything in this
    house is the \r\nwrong shade of brown. Samuel, meanwhile, has developed a \r\nhabit
    of sleeping with his bedroom door open. \r\nI should be so lucky to have so happy
    a household. \r\n18 September \r\nSamuel woke us last night. \r\nHe insists that
    something is standing at the end of his bed late \r\nat night. A man, apparently,
    although I hesitate to call it that. \r\nHe saw only its silhouette, and while
    its upper half is mostly \r\nhumanoid, its spine extends past its pelvis into
    a tail that drags \r\non the ground. Rather lovely imagery for a horror piece,
    I \r\nshould say. \r\nNeema explained that it was likely a sleep paralysis demon,
    a \r\nvivid hallucination caused when one regains consciousness \r\nwhile their
    body\u2019s natural muscle paralysis remains active.  \r\nIt did little to calm
    the boy. "
--- !u!114 &8366952609067242450
