  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 367689ee5044f384f90357a5791dcf2e, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::JournalItem
  journalText: "Journal \r\n3 October 2006 - 27 October 2006 \r\nHamish Abercrombie
    \r\n3 October \r\nTulia has been drawing Samuel\u2019s obsession. \r\nNeema found
    several sketches beneath her mattress while \r\ndoing laundry. They are remarkably
    consistent: a narrow, \r\nelongated body, a skull-like visage, and something
    akin to a \r\nspine trailing behind it.  \r\nShe claims she has never seen it
    herself; Samuel\u2019s \r\ndescriptions of it were so vivid that she could picture
    it. \r\nThey unnerved Neema, so much so that she suggested I burn \r\nthem in
    the yard.  \r\nI haven\u2019t yet. \r\n11 October \r\nJames has been taking measurements
    of the house. \r\nApparently, he believes the house is larger than the \r\narchitectural
    plans suggest. I told him that old houses are \r\nrarely built to mathematical
    perfection. \r\nHe disagreed. \r\nHe has become rather interested in finding
    the original \r\narchitectural plans of the house. I have instructed him not
    to \r\nbother.  \r\nThere are some things in this house that are best left alone."
--- !u!33 &8949966339426876600
