--- !u!114 &8949966339426876601
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1408623581329252072}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 367689ee5044f384f90357a5791dcf2e, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::JournalItem
  journalText: "Journal \r\n29 October 2006 - 15 November 2006 \r\nHamish Abercrombie
    \r\n29 October \r\nNeema found blood on Samuel\u2019s bedsheets this morning.
    Not \r\nmuch; a few spots, and Samuel reluctantly admitted that he \r\nhas been
    scratching himself in his sleep.  \r\nI found three long, albeit faint, marks
    across his bedroom \r\ndoor. They begin roughly four feet from the door and \r\ncontinue
    downwards.  \r\nThey are on the outside.  \r\nNeema took the boy to the hospital
    and returned that \r\nafternoon to say the results were inconclusive. There were
    \r\nno obvious signs of illness, although she says his \r\ntemperature has been
    fluctuating.  \r\nTulia thinks we should see someone else about it. I have \r\nalways
    loved the idea of grand, fantastical worlds, dragons, \r\nwizards, and what have
    you, but I have never been a \r\nsuperstitious man.  \r\nThat trait is becoming
    unwieldy.  \r\n13 November \r\nSamuel is no longer sleeping in his bedroom; Neema
    has \r\nmoved him into ours. She says the boy is frightened enough \r\nwithout
    us indulging his imagination. \r\nI cannot shake the feeling that something has
    changed in the \r\nhouse. The hallway seems longer at night. I measured it this
    \r\nafternoon. \r\nIt has not changed."
